  "notes": [
    "High-side switch: source to the supply, drain to the load; pull the gate to the source (100 kohm) so it stays off, and pull it low (an NPN or N-MOSFET such as 2N7002, or a GPIO when the supply is the GPIO's own) to turn it on. A 3.3 V GPIO can switch a 3.3 V rail directly; a 5 V rail needs the level shift.",
    "Reverse-polarity protection: drain to the input connector, source to the circuit, gate to GND (with a zener from gate to source above 12 V supplies): the body diode conducts first, then the channel shorts it.",
    "125 °C/W steady state: keep it under about 1 W at 25 °C ambient, with copper on the drain."
  ],
